("v26", "type", "String")
("v26", "scalar", "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: wide editorial illustration for Aaron Alderman's personal website, about a kenotic programme titled Power Must Serve Life. Create an evocative panoramic 3:2 composition in mixed graphite, charcoal, soft coloured pencil and wax crayon on warm ivory art paper. The visual moves from darkness on the left into light on the right: the left quarter contains an enclosed monumental geometric structure, intricate machinery and densely layered shadow, suggestive of concentrated technological power; across the middle, its rigid geometry opens into arches, pathways and a spacious living landscape. On the right, a warm sunlit shared world of modest workshops, open books, gardens, branching paths, trees and small ordinary human figures learning, making and caring together. Real architectural and landscape detail, sophisticated literary book illustration, thoughtful and beautiful rather than utopian propaganda. The people retain small independent places and purposes. Charcoal, smoky indigo, rust-red crayon accents, muted sage, pale ochre and warm cream. Rich visible handmade grain, delicate linework, organic irregular edges and areas of unmarked paper. Keep the composition legible at website sizes, no central robot, no humanoid AI, no glowing brain, no interface, no text, no lettering, no religious icon used as triumphal emblem, no logos or watermark. Image only, not a website mockup.")
("v25", "value", "v26")
("rel.document", "root", "v0")
